<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish new car licensings fall to 1,946 in December.</title>
<headline>Irish new car licensings fall to 1,946 in December.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of new private cars licensed in Ireland fell to 1,946 in December 1996 from 3,768 in November, provisional Central Statistics Office (CSO) data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Licensings were up from December 1995 when they totalled 996.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
